  "notes": [
    "New chat opens a conversation at once (routes/Chat.svelte, startConversation, commit 3d641da0a); the picker (new-chat-picker, quickpicker) shows only when create_chat_session fails. Two blocks still need the picker with a real model, its rewrite and its plan-mode checkbox: each arms a create_chat_session stub that rejects once, presses New chat, and clears the stub as soon as the picker is there, so quickpicker-submit creates the conversation for real and sends the first message. Every other fresh session is made as the screen does it now: the open conversation is closed first (chat-close-button, then its header gone) so the header awaited next is the new one, New chat, then the first message from the composer. chat-plan-mode-chip is awaited before that message because the header renders it only once the detail of the conversation is loaded (ChatConversationHeader.svelte, {#if session}), which is also when the conversation is pushed into currentSession, the store awaitTurn reads the session id from; closing a conversation clears that store (ChatConversation.svelte, onDestroy).",
    "ChatPlanHost picks the review card on the developer mode (ChatPlanHost.svelte): off, ChatPlanReview (chat-plan-review, with request-changes and an adjust textarea); on, ChatPlanReviewBuilder (chat-plan-review-builder, approve or reject only, revision by continuing to type). This block is written for the first card, so developer mode is turned off first (settings, settings-nav-developer, developer-mode-off) instead of inheriting whatever the previous section left. The settings open in a window above the chat, which stays mounted: the conversation is still the one shown when the window is left.",
    "The journey now ends on an approval: propose, request changes, revise, approve. Stopping after the revision left the plan pending forever and never exercised the gate that releases execution.",
    "The turn that follows the plan approval keeps the runner's default approval budget (25), not the 6 used while reviewing the plan: approving releases the execution of every planned step, and a three-step plan with two or three tools each blows past 6 approvals and aborts as a runaway turn.",
    "The ask_user card is answered from the To review screen, not from the chat card: AskUserCard's ask-user-submit is disabled until a question is answered and the model picks the question type, so no fixed step can enable it. The screen lists the question as a ReviewQuestionCard (components/inbox/ReviewQuestionCard.svelte): the prompt asks for a first name, an open question, so review-question-input- is filled and review-question-submit sent; the answer is held six seconds (ANSWER_HOLD_MS, reviewModel.ts) as review-answered, then sent. Before that, review-filter-questions narrows the list and review-open returns to the conversation, which leaves the request pending (Inbox.svelte open: pendingChatSessionId then navigateTo chat). A model that asks a choice question instead leaves review-question-input- absent and the block red: that is the model, not a broken anchor.",
    "The chat screen unmounts on a change of route (the key on the route in lib/components/app/Main.svelte) while the panes are a store, so going back to chat is expected to show the conversation again; the book does not rely on it and returns to the session it just left through conversation-row-menu-button nth 0 then conversation-row-menu-configure (openConfig then navigateToSession in routes/Chat.svelte; the default sort is newest created first, so row 0 is the newest session). That path also opens the right panel on its Settings tab; chat-config-button is openConfig() too, not a toggle, so pressing it again leaves the panel open.",
    "The developer plan card (chat-plan-review-builder) is reached with developer mode on and a conversation started in plan mode from the picker (quickpicker-plan-mode, a native checkbox, so setChecked). awaitTurn yields on that card since the runner's planCss lists it next to chat-plan-review (runner.ts, awaitTurn). Reject sends rejectPlan without a reason; if the model proposes a new plan right after, the following awaitTurn yields on the pending card and the section leaves it pending when it closes the conversation, which does not block the ask_user section (new session).",
    "chat-streaming-text is clicked while the answer streams: the span renders only once text arrives ({#if textContent || !activeThinking}, StreamingMessage.svelte:172), so the prompt asks for twenty sentences to keep the window open; the click itself is inert on plain text (StreamingText.svelte:33-51 acts on links and copy buttons only).",
    "chat-scroll-to-bottom appears only after an upward scroll leaves the list more than 200 px from the bottom (scrollFollow.ts:42-45, :63-75). The runner's click calls scrollIntoView({block:'center'}) on its target (runner.ts:228-230), so clicking the first message's copy button scrolls the list up; after nine turns the list overflows enough. The copy click also copies that message to the host clipboard.",
    "chat-stop-button is played once, on a long prompt, right before the plan section's new chat: the aborted session keeps a truncated assistant message and nothing after it reads that session again.",
    "The two rewrite blocks (quickpicker-rewrite-restore-button, chat-input-rewrite-restore-button) each cost one meta-LLM call on the default backend; restore is rendered only after a successful rewrite (canRestore) and emptying the field resets it (QuickPicker.svelte, ChatInput.svelte). A rewrite refused by the backend (noRouter/noBackend/callFailed/emptyAnswer) leaves the button absent and the block red without blocking the rest.",
    "hitl-always-toggle open/close is played by hitl-critical, not folded here (chat-llm keeps no approval pending).",
    "Measured on 2026-09-06 (two runs): the execution of the approved plan ended in an ask_user question the book never answers, which then made every later awaitTurn return 'paused for ask_user' at once and hid the plan review of the builder section and the twelve-reads turn. The plan prompts now forbid questions. Product finding for the maintainer: that question reached the inbox without a session id (the plan executor builds its ask_user executor without a session, apollia-tools native_dispatcher.rs), so the inbox row carried no 'open the conversation' action.",
    "The reasoning list's show-more and collapse are not played here: they need more than ten items in one turn, which depends on how many steps the model takes. chat-det plays them on a seeded turn instead.",
    "Timeouts are sized for a model that reasons before it answers (about 30 tokens per second on a 30B model): five minutes for a plain turn, a rewrite or the first streamed text, ten for a turn that calls tools or runs a plan. awaitTurn returns as soon as the turn settles, so a long deadline costs nothing on a green run. No step asserts the wording of an answer.",
    "chat-config-button is pressed before chat-inspector-plan-tab: the right panel is closed by default (routes/Chat.svelte renders it on contextDrawerOpen) and the tab exists only while it is open; the press is openConfig(), which opens it whatever its state."
  ]
}
